      "dom_id": "question-80060",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Solve the equation $2s+5{s}^{2}=s+4{s}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2s+5{s}^{2} & =s+4{s}^{2} \\\\ 2s+5{s}^{2}-(s+4{s}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2s+5{s}^{2}-s-4{s}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (5{s}^{2}-4{s}^{2})+(2s-s) & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}+s & =0 \\\\ s(s+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\ns=0\\,\\text{or}\\,s+1=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\ns=0\\,\\text{or}\\,s=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $s=-1,0.$",
