      "problem": "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $-7{d}^{2}=-49d$ are $d=${{field-1}} and $d=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7{d}^{2} & =-49d \\\\ -7{d}^{2}+49d & =0 \\\\ -7d(d-7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\n-7d=0\\,\\text{or}\\,d-7=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nd=0\\,\\text{or}\\,d=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $d=0$ and $d=7.$",
